id: energy-cancel
name: Energy Cancel
type: counter
actionCost: 1
kiCost: 0
usageLimit: 1/round
cancelCharge: true
source: Core Rule
description: >
  Plans change. Standing around charging an attack did not work, so change
  strategies immediately, even if you will lose the stamina you dedicated to
  charging.
text: >
  If you are currently suffering from the effects of the Energy Charge Maneuver
  when you are targeted by an Attacking Maneuver (or at the start of your turn),
  you can use this Maneuver to immediately lose all Energy Charges gained from
  the Energy Charge Maneuver but also stop suffering from the other effects of
  the Energy Charge Maneuver.

---

# No script, for the same reason the Energy Charge Maneuver has none: what this
# does is undo a declaration that is being held open, and a script has no way to
# reach one. `cancelCharge: true` hands it to the code that does.
#
# What it comes to:
#   - only offered while you are actually charging - there is nothing to cancel
#     otherwise, and a Maneuver that costs an Action to do nothing is a trap
#   - every Energy Charge on the declared attack is lost
#   - the declaration goes with them, and so does the Guard Down it was causing
#     and the hold on your other Attacking and Standard Maneuvers
#
# Two ways in, both named by the rule: from the card of an Attacking Maneuver
# aimed at you, and from your own sheet at the start of your turn.
#
# On the card it sits among the Counter Maneuvers, because that is what it costs -
# one Counter Action, and you only get to spend one answering any one Maneuver.
# So it is exclusive with the Defend Maneuver. It is not exclusive with dodging:
# a Dodge costs nothing, so having spent the Action here you dodge as you would
# have if you had spent nothing.
